with independent 30 percent failures the success rate rises from 70 to about 90 percent (0.7 + 0.3 x 0.7 = 91 percent expected), at the price of some answers coming from the weaker model; real provider outages are correlated, so treat this as the best case

--- 6. Genuinely checking: composite storage and the observability store ---
isolate_traces=False trace store down -> request failed: trace store unavailable | session saved: False
isolate_traces=True  trace store down -> request completed | session saved: True
when the trace write came first and was not isolated, an outage in the observability store lost the user's session update
append-only trace rows are cheap: 200000 rows in 0.06s, while sessions stay tiny: that asymmetry is the argument for separate stores"}},{"type":"heading","data":{"textEn":"Experiment Walkthrough","textKn":"Experiment ನಡೆದಾಟ","level":"H2"}},{"type":"concept","data":{"headingEn":"Experiment 1: Schema at the tool boundary","headingKn":"ಪ್ರಯೋಗ 1: Schema at the tool boundary","bodyEn":"What it ran: Schema at the tool boundary. What the lab concluded: None                                           SchemaError: input: expected object, got NoneType","bodyKn":"ಇದು ಓಡಿಸಿದ್ದು: Schema at the tool boundary. ಲ್ಯಾಬ್ ತೀರ್ಮಾನ (ಮೂಲ ಇಂಗ್ಲಿಷ್ ಪಠ್ಯ ಯಥಾವತ್ತಾಗಿ): None                                           SchemaError: input: expected object, got NoneType"}},{"type":"output","data":{"output":"--- 1. Schema at the tool boundary ---
