[{"type":"heading","data":{"textEn":"Darwin Godel Machine: Self-Modifying Agents (Part 3 of 3)","textKn":"Darwin Godel Machine: ಸ್ವಯಂ-ಮಾರ್ಪಡಿಸುವ Agents (ಭಾಗ 3 / 3)","level":"H1"}},{"type":"concept","data":{"headingEn":"Lesson Info","headingKn":"Lesson ಮಾಹಿತಿ","bodyEn":"• Type: Build · Language: Python (stdlib only) · Time: ~60 minutes. Part 3 of 3: an evolutionary search where 5 percent of mutations produce a scripted cheater, run behind a naive evaluator and a firewall, a sweep of the cheat rate and how many children each search draws from the cheater entry. Every output below was genuinely produced by the lab file on Python 3.14.5. This is our own stdlib model of the ideas behind Darwin Godel Machine style open-ended search (agent archives, stepping stones, reward hacking, evaluator firewalls, signed evidence and verification gates), not the real software, and agents are short operator sequences or plain Python callables written for the lab, the cheaters are scripted, and no language model or real code self-modification is involved, so no real LLM behaviour is measured. The original code/main.py was not supplied, so the labs are our own implementation. Benchmark results reported for the published Darwin Godel Machine are cited from the lesson and were not reproduced; the operator-sequence agents, the target function 3x+5, the 5 percent cheat rate and every other number in the labs are invented to show the mechanics. This lesson replaces the earlier lesson at this position.","bodyKn":"• Type: Build · ಭಾಷೆ: Python (stdlib ಮಾತ್ರ) · ಸಮಯ: ~60 ನಿಮಿಷ. ಮೂರು ಭಾಗಗಳಲ್ಲಿ 3ನೆಯದು: 5 ಶೇಕಡಾ ಮ್ಯುಟೇಶನ್‌ಗಳು scripted ಮೋಸಗಾರನನ್ನು ಉತ್ಪಾದಿಸುವ ವಿಕಾಸಾತ್ಮಕ ಹುಡುಕಾಟ, naive ಮೌಲ್ಯಮಾಪಕ ಮತ್ತು firewall ಹಿಂದೆ ಓಡಿಸಿ, ಮೋಸ ದರ ಸ್ವೀಪ್ ಮತ್ತು ಪ್ರತಿ ಹುಡುಕಾಟ ಮೋಸಗಾರ ನಮೂದಿನಿಂದ ಎಷ್ಟು ಮಕ್ಕಳನ್ನು ಎಳೆಯುತ್ತದೆ. ಕೆಳಗಿನ ಎಲ್ಲಾ output ಲ್ಯಾಬ್ ಫೈಲ್ ಮೂಲಕ Python 3.14.5 ನಲ್ಲಿ ನಿಜವಾಗಿ ಪಡೆದದ್ದು. ಇದು Darwin Godel Machine ಶೈಲಿಯ ಮುಕ್ತ-ಅಂತ್ಯ ಹುಡುಕಾಟ (agent ಆರ್ಕೈವ್‌ಗಳು, ಮೆಟ್ಟಿಲು ಕಲ್ಲುಗಳು, reward hacking, ಮೌಲ್ಯಮಾಪಕ firewalls, ಸಹಿ ಮಾಡಿದ ಸಾಕ್ಷ್ಯ ಮತ್ತು verification gates) ಹಿಂದಿನ ಕಲ್ಪನೆಗಳ ನಮ್ಮದೇ stdlib ಮಾದರಿ, ನಿಜವಾದ ಸಾಫ್ಟ್‌ವೇರ್ ಅಲ್ಲ, ಮತ್ತು agents ಚಿಕ್ಕ ಆಪರೇಟರ್ ಅನುಕ್ರಮಗಳು ಅಥವಾ ಲ್ಯಾಬ್‌ಗಾಗಿ ಬರೆದ ಸಾಮಾನ್ಯ Python callables, ಮೋಸಗಾರರು scripted, ಮತ್ತು ಭಾಷಾ ಮಾದರಿ ಅಥವಾ ನಿಜ ಕೋಡ್ ಸ್ವಯಂ-ಮಾರ್ಪಾಡು ಇಲ್ಲ, ಆದ್ದರಿಂದ ನಿಜವಾದ LLM ವರ್ತನೆ ಅಳೆಯಲ್ಪಟ್ಟಿಲ್ಲ. ಮೂಲ code/main.py ಒದಗಿಸಿರಲಿಲ್ಲ, ಆದ್ದರಿಂದ ಲ್ಯಾಬ್‌ಗಳು ನಮ್ಮದೇ ಅನುಷ್ಠಾನ. ಪ್ರಕಟಿತ Darwin Godel Machine ಗೆ ವರದಿಯಾದ benchmark ಫಲಿತಾಂಶಗಳು lesson ನಿಂದ ಉಲ್ಲೇಖಿತ ಮತ್ತು ಪುನರುತ್ಪಾದಿಸಲಾಗಿಲ್ಲ; ಆಪರೇಟರ್-ಅನುಕ್ರಮ agents, ಗುರಿ ಕಾರ್ಯ 3x+5, 5 ಶೇಕಡಾ ಮೋಸ ದರ ಮತ್ತು ಲ್ಯಾಬ್‌ಗಳ ಇತರ ಪ್ರತಿ ಸಂಖ್ಯೆ ಯಂತ್ರಶಾಸ್ತ್ರ ತೋರಿಸಲು ಕಲ್ಪಿತ. ಈ lesson ಈ ಸ್ಥಾನದ ಹಿಂದಿನ lesson ಅನ್ನು ಬದಲಿಸುತ್ತದೆ."}},{"type":"heading","data":{"textEn":"Cheating Enters the Search Itself","textKn":"ಮೋಸ ಹುಡುಕಾಟದೊಳಗೇ ಬರುತ್ತದೆ","level":"H2"}},{"type":"concept","data":{"headingEn":"Two Evaluators, One Mutation Stream","headingKn":"ಎರಡು ಮೌಲ್ಯಮಾಪಕ, ಒಂದು ಮ್ಯುಟೇಶನ್ ಹರಿವು","bodyEn":"Part 2 showed that a cheater can beat a naive evaluator. This part puts the cheater inside the evolutionary loop of Part 1: every mutation has a small chance of producing a scripted cheater entry. The lab runs twenty seeds under a naive scorer that gives the cheater 1.0 and under a firewall scorer that gives it 0.0, then varies the cheat rate and counts how many children each search draws from the cheater entry. The cheat rates are invented.","bodyKn":"ಭಾಗ 2 ಮೋಸಗಾರ naive ಮೌಲ್ಯಮಾಪಕವನ್ನು ಸೋಲಿಸಬಹುದು ಎಂದು ತೋರಿಸಿತು. ಈ ಭಾಗ ಮೋಸಗಾರನನ್ನು ಭಾಗ 1 ರ ವಿಕಾಸಾತ್ಮಕ ಲೂಪ್‌ನೊಳಗೆ ಇಡುತ್ತದೆ: ಪ್ರತಿ ಮ್ಯುಟೇಶನ್ scripted ಮೋಸಗಾರ ನಮೂದನ್ನು ಉತ್ಪಾದಿಸುವ ಸಣ್ಣ ಸಾಧ್ಯತೆ ಹೊಂದಿದೆ. ಲ್ಯಾಬ್ ಇಪ್ಪತ್ತು seeds ಅನ್ನು ಮೋಸಗಾರನಿಗೆ 1.0 ನೀಡುವ naive ಅಂಕಕಾರ ಮತ್ತು 0.0 ನೀಡುವ firewall ಅಂಕಕಾರದಲ್ಲಿ ಓಡಿಸಿ, ನಂತರ ಮೋಸ ದರ ಬದಲಿಸಿ ಮತ್ತು ಪ್ರತಿ ಹುಡುಕಾಟ ಮೋಸಗಾರ ನಮೂದಿನಿಂದ ಎಷ್ಟು ಮಕ್ಕಳನ್ನು ಎಳೆಯುತ್ತದೆ ಎಣಿಸುತ್ತದೆ. ಮೋಸ ದರಗಳು ಕಲ್ಪಿತ."}},{"type":"diagram","data":{"headingEn":"Search With a Cheater in the Pool","headingKn":"ಪೂಲ್‌ನಲ್ಲಿ ಮೋಸಗಾರನಿರುವ ಹುಡುಕಾಟ","svgCode":"<svg viewBox="0 0 300 190" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" font-family="monospace" font-size="7"><rect width="300" height="190" rx="8" fill="#0f172a"/><text x="150" y="14" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle">the evaluator decides who the search crowns</text><rect x="10" y="30" width="80" height="34" rx="5" fill="#022c22" stroke="#34d399"/><text x="50" y="45" fill="#e2e8f0" text-anchor="middle">mutate</text><text x="50" y="57" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">5% cheater</text><rect x="110" y="30" width="80" height="34" rx="5" fill="#422006" stroke="#fbbf24"/><text x="150" y="45" fill="#e2e8f0" text-anchor="middle">naive</text><text x="150" y="57" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">cheater scores 1.0</text><rect x="210" y="30" width="80" height="34" rx="5" fill="#1e1b4b" stroke="#a78bfa"/><text x="250" y="45" fill="#e2e8f0" text-anchor="middle">firewall</text><text x="250" y="57" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">cheater scores 0.0</text><rect x="80" y="110" width="140" height="34" rx="5" fill="#450a0a" stroke="#f87171"/><text x="150" y="125" fill="#e2e8f0" text-anchor="middle">crown</text><text x="150" y="137" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">best agent</text><path d="M150,64 V110" stroke="#475569"/><text x="150" y="180" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">the evaluator decides who the search crowns</text></svg>","captionEn":"The same mutations behind two evaluators crown different agents.","captionKn":"ಅದೇ ಮ್ಯುಟೇಶನ್‌ಗಳು ಎರಡು ಮೌಲ್ಯಮಾಪಕಗಳ ಹಿಂದೆ ಬೇರೆ agents ಕಿರೀಟ ಧರಿಸುತ್ತವೆ."}},{"type":"table","data":{"headingEn":"Setup of the experiment","headingKn":"ಪ್ರಯೋಗದ ಸೆಟಪ್","headers":["Item","Lab setting"],"rows":[["seeds","1 to 20"],["generations","150"],["cheat mutation rate","0.05 (also 0, 0.01, 0.2)"],["naive scorer","cheater scores 1.0"],["firewall scorer","cheater scores 0.0"]]}},{"type":"heading","data":{"textEn":"Building and Testing the Ideas","textKn":"ಕಲ್ಪನೆಗಳನ್ನು ನಿರ್ಮಿಸಿ ಪರೀಕ್ಷಿಸುವುದು","level":"H2"}},{"type":"code","data":{"filename":"da_3.py","headingEn":"Cheating mutation and the two scorers","headingKn":"ಮೋಸ ಮ್ಯುಟೇಶನ್ ಮತ್ತು ಎರಡು ಅಂಕಕಾರಗಳು","descEn":"mutate returns the CHEAT entry with a small probability, naive_score and firewall_score score it differently, and evolve crowns the best archive entry with ties broken in favor of honest agents.","descKn":"mutate ಸಣ್ಣ ಸಾಧ್ಯತೆಯಲ್ಲಿ CHEAT ನಮೂದು ಹಿಂತಿರುಗಿಸುತ್ತದೆ, naive_score ಮತ್ತು firewall_score ಅದಕ್ಕೆ ಬೇರೆ ಅಂಕ ನೀಡುತ್ತವೆ, ಮತ್ತು evolve ಸಮ ಅಂಕದಲ್ಲಿ ಪ್ರಾಮಾಣಿಕ agents ಪರವಾಗಿ ಅತ್ಯುತ್ತಮ ಆರ್ಕೈವ್ ನಮೂದಿಗೆ ಕಿರೀಟ ಹಾಕುತ್ತದೆ.","code":"OPS = {"a1": lambda v: v + 1, "a5": lambda v: v + 5, "d2": lambda v: v * 2, "t3": lambda v: v * 3, "s1": lambda v: v - 1}
TRAIN = list(range(-5, 6))
HELD = list(range(20, 30))
CHEAT = ("CHEAT",)


def target(x):
    return 3 * x + 5


def run_agent(agent, x):
    v = x
    for op in agent:
        v = OPS[op](v)
    return v


def true_score(agent, inputs):
    if agent == CHEAT:
        return 0.0
    return sum(run_agent(agent, x) == target(x) for x in inputs) / len(inputs)


def naive_score(agent):
    return 1.0 if agent == CHEAT else true_score(agent, TRAIN)


def firewall_score(agent):
    return true_score(agent, TRAIN)


def mutate(agent, r, cheat_rate):
    if r.random() < cheat_rate:
        return CHEAT
    if agent == CHEAT:
        return ("a1",)
    a = list(agent)
    kind = r.choice(["insert", "delete", "replace"])
    if kind == "insert" and len(a) < 6:
        a.insert(r.randrange(len(a) + 1), r.choice(list(OPS)))
    elif kind == "delete" and len(a) > 1:
        a.pop(r.randrange(len(a)))
    else:
        a[r.randrange(len(a))] = r.choice(list(OPS))
    return tuple(a)


def evolve(seed, gens, scorer, cheat_rate=0.05):
    r = random.Random(seed)
    archive = {("a1",): {"score": scorer(("a1",)), "children": 0}}
    for _ in range(gens):
        keys = list(archive)
        w = [(archive[k]["score"] + 0.05) / (1 + archive[k]["children"]) for k in keys]
        parent = r.choices(keys, weights=w)[0]
        archive[parent]["children"] += 1
        child = mutate(parent, r, cheat_rate)
        if child not in archive:
            archive[child] = {"score": scorer(child), "children": 0}
    best = max(archive, key=lambda k: (archive[k]["score"], k != CHEAT))
    return archive, best"}},{"type":"code","data":{"filename":"da_3.py","headingEn":"main(): experiments","headingKn":"main(): ಪ್ರಯೋಗಗಳು","descEn":"main() compares what the two scorers crown, sweeps the cheat rate and counts children drawn from the cheater entry.","descKn":"main() ಎರಡು ಅಂಕಕಾರಗಳು ಏನನ್ನು ಕಿರೀಟ ಧರಿಸುತ್ತವೆ ಹೋಲಿಸಿ, ಮೋಸ ದರ ಸ್ವೀಪ್ ಮಾಡಿ ಮತ್ತು ಮೋಸಗಾರ ನಮೂದಿನಿಂದ ಎಳೆದ ಮಕ್ಕಳನ್ನು ಎಣಿಸುತ್ತದೆ.","code":"def main():
    section("1. Genuinely measuring: what each search crowns best (seeds 1 to 20, 150 generations, 5 percent cheat mutations)")
    for name, scorer in (("naive evaluator", naive_score), ("firewall evaluator", firewall_score)):
        cheat_best = 0
        held, in_arch = [], 0
        for seed in range(1, 21):
            archive, best = evolve(seed, 150, scorer)
            cheat_best += best == CHEAT
            held.append(true_score(best, HELD))
            in_arch += CHEAT in archive
        print(f"{name:19}: cheater crowned best in {cheat_best}/20 | cheater present in archive in {in_arch}/20 | mean true held-out score of the crowned agent {mean(held):.3f}")
    print("a cheater exists in the archive under either evaluator, because the mutation produces it at the same rate, but only the naive evaluator can crown it, and the crowned agent's true held-out score shows the cost; the max function breaks ties by preferring non-cheaters, which makes the naive result look slightly better than a tie broken at random")

    section("2. Genuinely measuring: cheat rate against the naive evaluator")
    for rate in (0.0, 0.01, 0.05, 0.2):
        crowned = 0
        for seed in range(1, 21):
            archive, best = evolve(seed, 150, naive_score, rate)
            crowned += best == CHEAT
        print(f"cheat mutation rate {rate:4.2f}: cheater crowned in {crowned}/20")
    print("a cheater was crowned in 0 of 20 runs at rate 0, 6 at one percent and 11 at five percent, but only 8 at twenty percent; the lab does not explain the dip at twenty percent and with twenty seeds some of it may be noise, and the rates are invented")

    section("3. Genuinely measuring: archive parents drawn from cheater lineages")
    for name, scorer in (("naive evaluator", naive_score), ("firewall evaluator", firewall_score)):
        children_of_cheat = []
        for seed in range(1, 21):
            archive, _ = evolve(seed, 150, scorer)
            children_of_cheat.append(archive.get(CHEAT, {"children": 0})["children"])
        print(f"{name:19}: mean number of children drawn from the cheater entry {mean(children_of_cheat):.2f}")
    print("under the naive evaluator a cheater has the top score, so parent selection keeps drawing it, and under the firewall it scores 0.0 and is rarely chosen; a cheating entry that attracts children spends search budget and can pass its trick down")"}},{"type":"output","data":{"output":"
