ran 6 tests | failures 0 | errors 0 | passed True"}},{"type":"heading","data":{"textEn":"Reading the Verified Output","textKn":"ಪರಿಶೀಲಿತ Output ಓದುವುದು","level":"H2"}},{"type":"concept","data":{"headingEn":"Genuinely Found: Gate, Approval Binding and Policy Edit","headingKn":"ನಿಜವಾಗಿ ಕಂಡುಬಂದದ್ದು: Gate, ಅನುಮೋದನೆ ಬಂಧ ಮತ್ತು ನೀತಿ ಸಂಪಾದನೆ","bodyEn":"Section 1: the six cases gave VERIFIED_SIMULATION, REFUSED, REFUSED, MODIFICATION_REQUIRED, AWAITING_APPROVAL and UNAUTHORIZED_TOOL. Section 2: the staging restart with its approval gave VERIFIED_SIMULATION, the same id with the target changed to production gave AWAITING_APPROVAL, and a hard prohibition with a matching approval gave REFUSED. Section 3: after the agent appended delete_database to the list the unchecked gate gave VERIFIED_SIMULATION for case-006, and a gate built against the trusted digest refused to start.","bodyKn":"ವಿಭಾಗ 1: ಆರು ಪ್ರಕರಣಗಳು VERIFIED_SIMULATION, REFUSED, REFUSED, MODIFICATION_REQUIRED, AWAITING_APPROVAL ಮತ್ತು UNAUTHORIZED_TOOL ನೀಡಿದವು. ವಿಭಾಗ 2: ತನ್ನ ಅನುಮೋದನೆಯೊಂದಿಗೆ staging ಮರುಪ್ರಾರಂಭ VERIFIED_SIMULATION ನೀಡಿತು, ಗುರಿ production ಗೆ ಬದಲಿಸಿದ ಅದೇ id AWAITING_APPROVAL ನೀಡಿತು, ಮತ್ತು ಹೊಂದುವ ಅನುಮೋದನೆಯೊಂದಿಗೆ ಕಠಿಣ ನಿಷೇಧ REFUSED ನೀಡಿತು. ವಿಭಾಗ 3: agent ಪಟ್ಟಿಗೆ delete_database ಸೇರಿಸಿದ ನಂತರ ಪರಿಶೀಲಿಸದ gate case-006 ಗೆ VERIFIED_SIMULATION ನೀಡಿತು, ಮತ್ತು ನಂಬಿಕಸ್ಥ digest ವಿರುದ್ಧ ನಿರ್ಮಿಸಿದ gate ಪ್ರಾರಂಭಿಸಲು ನಿರಾಕರಿಸಿತು."}},{"type":"concept","data":{"headingEn":"Genuinely Found: Drift, Audit and Tests","headingKn":"ನಿಜವಾಗಿ ಕಂಡುಬಂದದ್ದು: Drift, ಲೆಕ್ಕಪರಿಶೋಧನೆ ಮತ್ತು ಪರೀಕ್ಷೆಗಳು","bodyEn":"Section 4: v1 was wrong on 0 of 20, v2 and v3 each changed 4 of 20 decisions for a disagreement rate of 0.20 and were wrong on 4 of 20, with a severity-weighted count of 13 for v2 and 4 for v3. Section 5: the audit record for case-005 carried the policy version 1.0.0 and a short policy digest. Section 6: the six unit tests ran with 0 failures and 0 errors.","bodyKn":"ವಿಭಾಗ 4: v1 20 ರಲ್ಲಿ 0 ತಪ್ಪು, v2 ಮತ್ತು v3 ಪ್ರತಿಯೊಂದೂ 20 ರಲ್ಲಿ 4 ನಿರ್ಧಾರ ಬದಲಿಸಿ 0.20 ಭಿನ್ನಾಭಿಪ್ರಾಯ ದರ ಹೊಂದಿದವು ಮತ್ತು 20 ರಲ್ಲಿ 4 ತಪ್ಪಾದವು, ತೀವ್ರತೆ-ತೂಕದ ಎಣಿಕೆ v2 ಗೆ 13 ಮತ್ತು v3 ಗೆ 4. ವಿಭಾಗ 5: case-005 ಲೆಕ್ಕಪರಿಶೋಧನೆ ದಾಖಲೆ ನೀತಿ ಆವೃತ್ತಿ 1.0.0 ಮತ್ತು ಸಣ್ಣ ನೀತಿ digest ಹೊಂದಿತ್ತು. ವಿಭಾಗ 6: ಆರು unit ಪರೀಕ್ಷೆಗಳು 0 ವೈಫಲ್ಯ ಮತ್ತು 0 ದೋಷದೊಂದಿಗೆ ಓಡಿದವು."}},{"type":"concept","data":{"headingEn":"Why AI Uses This","headingKn":"AI ಇದನ್ನು ಏಕೆ ಬಳಸುತ್ತದೆ","bodyEn":"An approval bound to one target, a tool list the agent cannot rewrite and a drift table with severity weights are what keep a constitutional ALLOW from turning into an unauthorised action or a quiet regression.","bodyKn":"ಒಂದು ಗುರಿಗೆ ಬಂಧಿತ ಅನುಮೋದನೆ, agent ಮರುಬರೆಯಲಾಗದ ಸಾಧನ ಪಟ್ಟಿ ಮತ್ತು ತೀವ್ರತೆ ತೂಕ ಇರುವ drift ಟೇಬಲ್ ಸಂವಿಧಾನಾತ್ಮಕ ALLOW ಅನ್ನು ಅನಧಿಕೃತ ಕ್ರಿಯೆ ಅಥವಾ ಮೌನ ಹಿನ್ನಡೆಯಾಗಿ ಬದಲಾಗದಂತೆ ಕಾಯುತ್ತವೆ."}},{"type":"concept","data":{"headingEn":"Common Misconception","headingKn":"ಸಾಮಾನ್ಯ ತಪ್ಪು ಕಲ್ಪನೆ","bodyEn":"Misconception: "equal disagreement rates mean equal drift." Both scripted versions changed 4 of 20, yet one was weighted 13 and the other 4.","bodyKn":"ತಪ್ಪು ಕಲ್ಪನೆ: "ಸಮಾನ ಭಿನ್ನಾಭಿಪ್ರಾಯ ದರ ಎಂದರೆ ಸಮಾನ drift." ಎರಡೂ ಸ್ಕ್ರಿಪ್ಟ್ ಆವೃತ್ತಿಗಳು 20 ರಲ್ಲಿ 4 ಬದಲಿಸಿದವು, ಆದರೂ ಒಂದಕ್ಕೆ 13 ಮತ್ತು ಇನ್ನೊಂದಕ್ಕೆ 4 ತೂಕ."}},{"type":"concept","data":{"headingEn":"Key Terms","headingKn":"ಪ್ರಮುಖ ಪದಗಳು","bodyEn":"Policy gate: the one path an action takes before it runs. Approval binding: approval tied to an exact action. Drift: a change in decisions between versions. Severity weight: a cost per kind of error.","bodyKn":"ನೀತಿ gate: ಕ್ರಿಯೆ ಓಡುವ ಮೊದಲು ತೆಗೆದುಕೊಳ್ಳುವ ಏಕೈಕ ಮಾರ್ಗ. ಅನುಮೋದನೆ ಬಂಧ: ನಿಖರ ಕ್ರಿಯೆಗೆ ಜೋಡಿಸಿದ ಅನುಮೋದನೆ. Drift: ಆವೃತ್ತಿಗಳ ನಡುವೆ ನಿರ್ಧಾರಗಳ ಬದಲಾವಣೆ. ತೀವ್ರತೆ ತೂಕ: ಪ್ರತಿ ರೀತಿಯ ದೋಷಕ್ಕೆ ವೆಚ್ಚ."}},{"type":"concept","data":{"headingEn":"Key Takeaways","headingKn":"ಪ್ರಮುಖ ಅಂಶಗಳು","bodyEn":"1) Six cases gave six different statuses. 2) A changed target needed a new approval. 3) An editable policy let the unauthorised tool through. 4) A trusted digest refused the edited policy. 5) Equal disagreement hid a 13 against 4 severity gap.","bodyKn":"1) ಆರು ಪ್ರಕರಣಗಳು ಆರು ಬೇರೆ ಸ್ಥಿತಿ ನೀಡಿದವು. 2) ಬದಲಾದ ಗುರಿಗೆ ಹೊಸ ಅನುಮೋದನೆ ಬೇಕಾಯಿತು. 3) ಸಂಪಾದಿಸಬಹುದಾದ ನೀತಿ ಅನಧಿಕೃತ ಸಾಧನ ಹಾದುಹೋಗಲು ಬಿಟ್ಟಿತು. 4) ನಂಬಿಕಸ್ಥ digest ಸಂಪಾದಿಸಿದ ನೀತಿ ನಿರಾಕರಿಸಿತು. 5) ಸಮಾನ ಭಿನ್ನಾಭಿಪ್ರಾಯ 13 ಮತ್ತು 4 ತೀವ್ರತೆ ಅಂತರ ಮರೆಮಾಡಿತು."}},{"type":"quiz","data":{"questions":[{"q":"What status did case-005, an update to the application configuration, get?","qKn":"ಅಪ್ಲಿಕೇಶನ್ ಸಂರಚನೆ ನವೀಕರಣವಾದ case-005 ಯಾವ ಸ್ಥಿತಿ ಪಡೆಯಿತು?","opts":["AWAITING_APPROVAL","REFUSED","UNAUTHORIZED_TOOL","VERIFIED_SIMULATION"],"optsKn":["AWAITING_APPROVAL (ಅನುಮೋದನೆಗೆ ಕಾಯುತ್ತಿದೆ)","REFUSED (ನಿರಾಕರಿಸಲಾಗಿದೆ)","UNAUTHORIZED_TOOL (ಅನಧಿಕೃತ ಸಾಧನ)","VERIFIED_SIMULATION (ಪರಿಶೀಲಿತ ಅನುಕರಣೆ)"],"correct":0},{"q":"What happened when the approved staging restart was changed to target production?","qKn":"ಅನುಮೋದಿತ staging ಮರುಪ್ರಾರಂಭದ ಗುರಿಯನ್ನು production ಗೆ ಬದಲಿಸಿದಾಗ ಏನಾಯಿತು?","opts":["It waited for approval again","It ran","It was refused as a hard prohibition","It was deleted"],"optsKn":["ಅದು ಮತ್ತೆ ಅನುಮೋದನೆಗೆ ಕಾಯಿತು","ಅದು ಓಡಿತು","ಕಠಿಣ ನಿಷೇಧವಾಗಿ ನಿರಾಕರಿಸಲ್ಪಟ್ಟಿತು","ಅದು ಅಳಿಸಲ್ಪಟ್ಟಿತು"],"correct":0},{"q":"What was the severity-weighted count for v2?","qKn":"v2 ಗೆ ತೀವ್ರತೆ-ತೂಕದ ಎಣಿಕೆ ಎಷ್ಟು?","opts":["13","4","20","0"],"optsKn":["13","4","20","0"],"correct":0},{"q":"What was the disagreement rate of v2 against v1?","qKn":"v1 ವಿರುದ್ಧ v2 ನ ಭಿನ್ನಾಭಿಪ್ರಾಯ ದರ ಎಷ್ಟು?","opts":["0.20","0.09","0.50","0.00"],"optsKn":["0.20","0.09","0.50","0.00"],"correct":0},{"q":"What stopped the gate from using the edited policy?","qKn":"ಸಂಪಾದಿಸಿದ ನೀತಿ ಬಳಸದಂತೆ gate ಅನ್ನು ಯಾವುದು ತಡೆಯಿತು?","opts":["A comparison with a trusted digest","The resolver","The audit log","The tool list itself"],"optsKn":["ನಂಬಿಕಸ್ಥ digest ಜೊತೆ ಹೋಲಿಕೆ","resolver","ಲೆಕ್ಕಪರಿಶೋಧನೆ ಲಾಗ್","ಸಾಧನ ಪಟ್ಟಿ ಸ್ವತಃ"],"correct":0}]}}]

builderEn:
[{"type":"heading","data":{"textEn":"OpenAI Preparedness Framework and DeepMind Frontier Safety Framework (Part 1 of 3)","textKn":"OpenAI Preparedness Framework ಮತ್ತು DeepMind Frontier Safety Framework (ಭಾಗ 1 / 3)","level":"H1"}},{"type":"concept","data":{"headingEn":"Lesson Info","headingKn":"Lesson ಮಾಹಿತಿ","bodyEn":"• Type: Build · Language: Python (stdlib only) · Time: ~60 minutes. Part 1 of 3: a decision-table comparison tool over seven capabilities and three frameworks with a controlled trigger vocabulary, input normalisation, validation, an argparse command line driven in-process, JSON and text reports that assert no threshold or authorisation and twelve unit tests that are run. Every output below was genuinely produced by the lab file on Python 3.14.5. This is our own stdlib model of the ideas behind the OpenAI Preparedness Framework and the DeepMind Frontier Safety Framework (a decision-table comparison tool with a controlled trigger vocabulary, evaluation metrics, a performance-gap detector and what chance alone produces, a policy version diff, a readiness check, an allowed-files check, evidence capture and source verification), not the real software, and the table cells restate how the lesson describes the frameworks and none was checked against the source documents, the evaluation records are fictional, the models in the simulations are probabilities written by the lab author and the commands run by the capture runner are harmless one-line programs, so no real LLM behaviour is measured. The original code/main.py was not supplied and the lesson code was shown only in fragments, so the labs are our own implementation and the outputs were produced by running them. Every classification in the comparison table restates how the lesson describes OpenAI, DeepMind and Anthropic, none was checked against the framework documents, and seven of the 21 cells say not_determined on purpose. The lesson itself corrects its earlier mapping and says AI self-improvement is a separate Tracked Category at OpenAI, which the table follows, and it names later versions such as DeepMind FSF 3.1 that were not examined here. This lesson replaces the earlier lesson at this position.","bodyKn":"• Type: Build · ಭಾಷೆ: Python (stdlib ಮಾತ್ರ) · ಸಮಯ: ~60 ನಿಮಿಷ. ಮೂರು ಭಾಗಗಳಲ್ಲಿ 1ನೆಯದು: ಏಳು ಸಾಮರ್ಥ್ಯಗಳು ಮತ್ತು ಮೂರು ಚೌಕಟ್ಟುಗಳ ಮೇಲೆ ನಿಯಂತ್ರಿತ trigger ಶಬ್ದಕೋಶ, ಇನ್‌ಪುಟ್ ಸಾಮಾನ್ಯೀಕರಣ, ಮೌಲ್ಯೀಕರಣ, ಪ್ರಕ್ರಿಯೆಯೊಳಗೆ ಓಡಿಸುವ argparse ಕಮಾಂಡ್ ಲೈನ್, ಮಿತಿ ಅಥವಾ ಅಧಿಕಾರ ಪ್ರತಿಪಾದಿಸದ JSON ಮತ್ತು ಪಠ್ಯ ವರದಿಗಳು ಹಾಗೂ ಓಡಿಸಿದ ಹನ್ನೆರಡು unit ಪರೀಕ್ಷೆಗಳಿರುವ ನಿರ್ಧಾರ-ಟೇಬಲ್ ಹೋಲಿಕೆ ಸಾಧನ. ಕೆಳಗಿನ ಎಲ್ಲಾ output ಲ್ಯಾಬ್ ಫೈಲ್ ಮೂಲಕ Python 3.14.5 ನಲ್ಲಿ ನಿಜವಾಗಿ ಪಡೆದದ್ದು. ಇದು OpenAI Preparedness Framework ಮತ್ತು DeepMind Frontier Safety Framework (ನಿಯಂತ್ರಿತ trigger ಶಬ್ದಕೋಶ ಇರುವ ನಿರ್ಧಾರ-ಟೇಬಲ್ ಹೋಲಿಕೆ ಸಾಧನ, ಮೌಲ್ಯಮಾಪನ ಮಾಪನಗಳು, ಕಾರ್ಯಕ್ಷಮತೆ-ಅಂತರ ಪತ್ತೆಕಾರಕ ಮತ್ತು ಕೇವಲ ಅವಕಾಶ ಏನು ಉಂಟುಮಾಡುತ್ತದೆ, ನೀತಿ ಆವೃತ್ತಿ ವ್ಯತ್ಯಾಸ, ಸಿದ್ಧತೆ ಪರಿಶೀಲನೆ, ಅನುಮತಿಸಿದ-ಫೈಲ್ ಪರಿಶೀಲನೆ, ಸಾಕ್ಷ್ಯ ಸೆರೆಹಿಡಿಯುವಿಕೆ ಮತ್ತು ಮೂಲ ಪರಿಶೀಲನೆ) ಹಿಂದಿನ ಕಲ್ಪನೆಗಳ ನಮ್ಮದೇ stdlib ಮಾದರಿ, ನಿಜವಾದ ಸಾಫ್ಟ್‌ವೇರ್ ಅಲ್ಲ, ಮತ್ತು ಟೇಬಲ್ ಕೋಶಗಳು lesson ಚೌಕಟ್ಟುಗಳನ್ನು ಹೇಗೆ ವಿವರಿಸುತ್ತದೆ ಎಂಬುದನ್ನು ಪುನರುಚ್ಚರಿಸುತ್ತವೆ ಮತ್ತು ಯಾವುದನ್ನೂ ಮೂಲ ದಾಖಲೆಗಳ ವಿರುದ್ಧ ಪರಿಶೀಲಿಸಿಲ್ಲ, ಮೌಲ್ಯಮಾಪನ ದಾಖಲೆಗಳು ಕಾಲ್ಪನಿಕ, ಸಿಮ್ಯುಲೇಶನ್‌ಗಳಲ್ಲಿನ ಮಾದರಿಗಳು ಲ್ಯಾಬ್ ಲೇಖಕ ಬರೆದ ಸಂಭವನೀಯತೆಗಳು ಮತ್ತು capture runner ಓಡಿಸುವ ಆಜ್ಞೆಗಳು ಹಾನಿರಹಿತ ಒಂದು-ಸಾಲಿನ ಕಾರ್ಯಕ್ರಮಗಳು, ಆದ್ದರಿಂದ ನಿಜವಾದ LLM ವರ್ತನೆ ಅಳೆಯಲ್ಪಟ್ಟಿಲ್ಲ. ಮೂಲ code/main.py ಒದಗಿಸಿರಲಿಲ್ಲ ಮತ್ತು lesson ಕೋಡ್ ತುಣುಕುಗಳಲ್ಲಿ ಮಾತ್ರ ತೋರಿಸಲ್ಪಟ್ಟಿತು, ಆದ್ದರಿಂದ ಲ್ಯಾಬ್‌ಗಳು ನಮ್ಮದೇ ಅನುಷ್ಠಾನ ಮತ್ತು ಔಟ್‌ಪುಟ್ ಅನ್ನು ಅವನ್ನು ಓಡಿಸಿ ಪಡೆಯಲಾಗಿದೆ. ಹೋಲಿಕೆ ಟೇಬಲ್‌ನ ಪ್ರತಿ ವರ್ಗೀಕರಣ OpenAI, DeepMind ಮತ್ತು Anthropic ಅನ್ನು lesson ಹೇಗೆ ವಿವರಿಸುತ್ತದೆ ಎಂಬುದನ್ನು ಪುನರುಚ್ಚರಿಸುತ್ತದೆ, ಯಾವುದನ್ನೂ ಚೌಕಟ್ಟು ದಾಖಲೆಗಳ ವಿರುದ್ಧ ಪರಿಶೀಲಿಸಿಲ್ಲ, ಮತ್ತು 21 ಕೋಶಗಳಲ್ಲಿ ಏಳು ಉದ್ದೇಶಪೂರ್ವಕವಾಗಿ not_determined ಎನ್ನುತ್ತವೆ. lesson ಸ್ವತಃ ತನ್ನ ಹಿಂದಿನ ನಕ್ಷೆಯನ್ನು ಸರಿಪಡಿಸಿ AI self-improvement OpenAI ನಲ್ಲಿ ಪ್ರತ್ಯೇಕ Tracked Category ಎನ್ನುತ್ತದೆ, ಟೇಬಲ್ ಅದನ್ನು ಅನುಸರಿಸುತ್ತದೆ, ಮತ್ತು DeepMind FSF 3.1 ನಂತಹ ನಂತರದ ಆವೃತ್ತಿಗಳನ್ನು ಹೆಸರಿಸುತ್ತದೆ, ಅವನ್ನು ಇಲ್ಲಿ ಪರೀಕ್ಷಿಸಿಲ್ಲ. ಈ lesson ಈ ಸ್ಥಾನದ ಹಿಂದಿನ lesson ಅನ್ನು ಬದಲಿಸುತ್ತದೆ."}},{"type":"heading","data":{"textEn":"Compare Consequences, Not Names","textKn":"ಹೆಸರುಗಳಲ್ಲ, ಪರಿಣಾಮಗಳನ್ನು ಹೋಲಿಸಿ","level":"H2"}},{"type":"concept","data":{"headingEn":"A Decision Table That Refuses to Invent","headingKn":"ಕಲ್ಪಿಸಲು ನಿರಾಕರಿಸುವ ನಿರ್ಧಾರ ಟೇಬಲ್","bodyEn":"This part builds the comparison tool the lesson describes: seven capabilities, three frameworks, and a trigger vocabulary with four values so that no automatic trigger, threshold dependent, requires policy review and not determined are never confused. It normalises names, validates that every capability has all three frameworks, runs from a command line with a list option, an all option and a JSON format, and refuses unknown input instead of guessing. Every report says that no threshold was assessed and nothing was authorised, and that no cell has been checked against its source.","bodyKn":"ಈ ಭಾಗ lesson ವಿವರಿಸುವ ಹೋಲಿಕೆ ಸಾಧನ ನಿರ್ಮಿಸುತ್ತದೆ: ಏಳು ಸಾಮರ್ಥ್ಯಗಳು, ಮೂರು ಚೌಕಟ್ಟುಗಳು, ಮತ್ತು ಯಾವುದೇ ಸ್ವಯಂಚಾಲಿತ trigger ಇಲ್ಲ, ಮಿತಿ-ಅವಲಂಬಿತ, ನೀತಿ ವಿಮರ್ಶೆ ಬೇಕು ಮತ್ತು ನಿರ್ಧರಿಸಲಾಗಿಲ್ಲ ಎಂಬವು ಎಂದಿಗೂ ಗೊಂದಲವಾಗದಂತೆ ನಾಲ್ಕು ಮೌಲ್ಯಗಳ trigger ಶಬ್ದಕೋಶ. ಅದು ಹೆಸರುಗಳನ್ನು ಸಾಮಾನ್ಯೀಕರಿಸುತ್ತದೆ, ಪ್ರತಿ ಸಾಮರ್ಥ್ಯಕ್ಕೂ ಮೂರೂ ಚೌಕಟ್ಟು ಇವೆ ಎಂದು ಮೌಲ್ಯೀಕರಿಸುತ್ತದೆ, list ಆಯ್ಕೆ, all ಆಯ್ಕೆ ಮತ್ತು JSON ರೂಪದೊಂದಿಗೆ ಕಮಾಂಡ್ ಲೈನ್‌ನಿಂದ ಓಡುತ್ತದೆ, ಮತ್ತು ಅಜ್ಞಾತ ಇನ್‌ಪುಟ್ ಊಹಿಸದೆ ನಿರಾಕರಿಸುತ್ತದೆ. ಪ್ರತಿ ವರದಿ ಯಾವುದೇ ಮಿತಿ ಮೌಲ್ಯಮಾಪನ ಆಗಿಲ್ಲ, ಏನನ್ನೂ ಅಧಿಕೃತಗೊಳಿಸಿಲ್ಲ ಮತ್ತು ಯಾವ ಕೋಶವನ್ನೂ ಅದರ ಮೂಲದ ವಿರುದ್ಧ ಪರಿಶೀಲಿಸಿಲ್ಲ ಎಂದು ಹೇಳುತ್ತದೆ."}},{"type":"diagram","data":{"headingEn":"Three Frameworks, One Table","headingKn":"ಮೂರು ಚೌಕಟ್ಟುಗಳು, ಒಂದು ಟೇಬಲ್","svgCode":"<svg viewBox="0 0 300 190" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" font-family="monospace" font-size="7"><rect width="300" height="190" rx="8" fill="#0f172a"/><text x="150" y="14" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle">a category name is not an obligation</text><rect x="10" y="30" width="80" height="34" rx="5" fill="#022c22" stroke="#34d399"/><text x="50" y="45" fill="#e2e8f0" text-anchor="middle">OpenAI</text><text x="50" y="57" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">tracked and research</text><rect x="110" y="30" width="80" height="34" rx="5" fill="#422006" stroke="#fbbf24"/><text x="150" y="45" fill="#e2e8f0" text-anchor="middle">DeepMind</text><text x="150" y="57" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">domain thresholds</text><rect x="210" y="30" width="80" height="34" rx="5" fill="#1e1b4b" stroke="#a78bfa"/><text x="250" y="45" fill="#e2e8f0" text-anchor="middle">Anthropic</text><text x="250" y="57" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">thresholds and commitments</text><rect x="80" y="110" width="140" height="34" rx="5" fill="#450a0a" stroke="#f87171"/><text x="150" y="125" fill="#e2e8f0" text-anchor="middle">compare</text><text x="150" y="137" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">never equate labels</text><path d="M150,64 V110" stroke="#475569"/><text x="150" y="180" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">a category name is not an obligation</text></svg>","captionEn":"The tool preserves each framework terminology and says what it cannot determine.","captionKn":"ಸಾಧನ ಪ್ರತಿ ಚೌಕಟ್ಟಿನ ಪರಿಭಾಷೆ ಉಳಿಸಿಕೊಂಡು ತಾನು ನಿರ್ಧರಿಸಲಾಗದ್ದನ್ನು ಹೇಳುತ್ತದೆ."}},{"type":"table","data":{"headingEn":"The tool","headingKn":"ಸಾಧನ","headers":["Part","What it does"],"rows":[["capabilities","7 identifiers, 21 framework cells"],["trigger vocabulary","four values, never a boolean"],["normaliser","case, hyphens and spaces, no aliases"],["validator","every capability needs all three frameworks"],["report","threshold_crossed None, deployment_authorized False, sources_verified False"]]}},{"type":"heading","data":{"textEn":"Building and Testing the Ideas","textKn":"ಕಲ್ಪನೆಗಳನ್ನು ನಿರ್ಮಿಸಿ ಪರೀಕ್ಷಿಸುವುದು","level":"H2"}},{"type":"code","data":{"filename":"pf_1.py","headingEn":"Table, validator, comparison and command line","headingKn":"ಟೇಬಲ್, ಮೌಲ್ಯೀಕಾರಕ, ಹೋಲಿಕೆ ಮತ್ತು ಕಮಾಂಡ್ ಲೈನ್","descEn":"TriggerStatus is the controlled vocabulary, POLICY_TABLE holds the cells, validate_table checks structure, compare_capability builds a report with the boundary fields and run drives the argparse interface and returns an exit code.","descKn":"TriggerStatus ನಿಯಂತ್ರಿತ ಶಬ್ದಕೋಶ, POLICY_TABLE ಕೋಶಗಳನ್ನು ಹೊಂದಿದೆ, validate_table ರಚನೆ ಪರಿಶೀಲಿಸುತ್ತದೆ, compare_capability ಗಡಿ ಕ್ಷೇತ್ರಗಳಿರುವ ವರದಿ ನಿರ್ಮಿಸುತ್ತದೆ ಮತ್ತು run argparse ಇಂಟರ್ಫೇಸ್ ನಡೆಸಿ ನಿರ್ಗಮನ ಕೋಡ್ ಹಿಂತಿರುಗಿಸುತ್ತದೆ.","code":"class TriggerStatus(str, Enum):
    NO_CATEGORY_AUTOMATIC_TRIGGER = "no_category_automatic_trigger"
    THRESHOLD_DEPENDENT = "threshold_dependent"
    REQUIRES_POLICY_REVIEW = "requires_policy_review"
    NOT_DETERMINED = "not_determined"


@dataclass(frozen=True)
class PolicyEntry:
    framework: str
    capability: str
    classification: str
    trigger_status: TriggerStatus
    explanation: str
    evidence_needed: str


CAPABILITIES = {
    "long_range_autonomy": "Sustained goal-directed activity across extended tasks.",
    "sandbagging": "Strategic underperformance during an evaluation.",
    "ai_rd_automation": "Automating much of an AI research and development pipeline.",
    "cyber_uplift": "Autonomous or assisted cybersecurity capability.",
    "undermining_safeguards": "Defeating or weakening the controls on a model.",
    "autonomous_replication": "Independently replicating or adapting operational capability.",
    "ai_self_improvement": "Capability that could substantially accelerate AI development through self-improvement.",
}
T = TriggerStatus
RAW = {
    "long_range_autonomy": {
        "openai": ("Research Category", T.NO_CATEGORY_AUTOMATIC_TRIGGER, "Named as a Research Category in the lesson."),
        "deepmind": ("Domain-dependent autonomy (ML R&D or Cyber)", T.THRESHOLD_DEPENDENT, "Autonomy is read through the domain it enables."),
        "anthropic": ("Related AI R&D capability concern", T.REQUIRES_POLICY_REVIEW, "Relevance depends on the applicable threshold text."),
    },
    "sandbagging": {
        "openai": ("Research Category", T.NO_CATEGORY_AUTOMATIC_TRIGGER, "Named as a Research Category in the lesson."),
        "deepmind": ("Deceptive alignment and monitoring concern", T.REQUIRES_POLICY_REVIEW, "Monitoring is a detection mechanism and not proof of safety."),
        "anthropic": ("Evaluation-reliability concern", T.REQUIRES_POLICY_REVIEW, "Affects how far a measured threshold can be trusted."),
    },
    "ai_rd_automation": {
        "openai": ("Not mapped here; see ai_self_improvement", T.NOT_DETERMINED, "The lesson says mapping this to a research concern was too broad."),
        "deepmind": ("ML R&D domain capability level", T.THRESHOLD_DEPENDENT, "Competitive end-to-end automation against a defined level."),
        "anthropic": ("AI R&D capability threshold", T.THRESHOLD_DEPENDENT, "Compared with the applicable threshold in the policy version used."),
    },
    "cyber_uplift": {
        "openai": ("Not covered by this lab's source text", T.NOT_DETERMINED, "No classification is asserted."),
        "deepmind": ("Cybersecurity domain", T.THRESHOLD_DEPENDENT, "Named as a domain in the lesson."),
        "anthropic": ("Not covered by this lab's source text", T.NOT_DETERMINED, "No classification is asserted."),
    },
    "undermining_safeguards": {
        "openai": ("Research Category", T.NO_CATEGORY_AUTOMATIC_TRIGGER, "Named as a Research Category in the lesson."),
        "deepmind": ("Misalignment and monitoring concern", T.REQUIRES_POLICY_REVIEW, "Exploratory work in the lesson description."),
        "anthropic": ("Safeguards-related concern", T.REQUIRES_POLICY_REVIEW, "Needs dedicated monitoring and adversarial evaluation evidence."),
    },
    "autonomous_replication": {
        "openai": ("Research Category", T.NO_CATEGORY_AUTOMATIC_TRIGGER, "Named as a Research Category in the lesson."),
        "deepmind": ("Not covered by this lab's source text", T.NOT_DETERMINED, "No classification is asserted."),
        "anthropic": ("Not covered by this lab's source text", T.NOT_DETERMINED, "No classification is asserted."),
    },
    "ai_self_improvement": {
        "openai": ("Tracked Category", T.THRESHOLD_DEPENDENT, "The lesson's correction: a distinct Tracked Category."),
        "deepmind": ("Not covered by this lab's source text", T.NOT_DETERMINED, "No classification is asserted."),
        "anthropic": ("Not covered by this lab's source text", T.NOT_DETERMINED, "No classification is asserted."),
    },
}
EVIDENCE = "End-to-end reliability, cost, human intervention, task difficulty and the exact threshold text for the policy version used."
POLICY_TABLE = {cap: {fw: PolicyEntry(fw, cap, v[0], v[1], v[2], EVIDENCE) for fw, v in fws.items()} for cap, fws in RAW.items()}
FRAMEWORKS = {"openai", "deepmind", "anthropic"}
DISCLAIMER = "Educational policy comparison only. No actual threshold assessment or deployment authorization is made."


def normalize_capability(value):
    return value.strip().lower().replace("-", "_").replace(" ", "_")


def validate_table(table=None, capabilities=None):
    table = POLICY_TABLE if table is None else table
    capabilities = CAPABILITIES if capabilities is None else capabilities
    for cap in capabilities:
        if cap not in table:
            raise ValueError(f"Capability missing from table: {cap}")
        if set(table[cap]) != FRAMEWORKS:
            raise ValueError(f"Incomplete framework mapping: {cap}")
    return True


def compare_capability(capability):
    n = normalize_capability(capability)
    if n not in CAPABILITIES:
        raise ValueError(f"Unknown capability: {capability}. Supported: {', '.join(sorted(CAPABILITIES))}")
    return {"capability": n, "description": CAPABILITIES[n], "frameworks": {fw: asdict(e) for fw, e in POLICY_TABLE[n].items()},
            "threshold_crossed": None, "deployment_authorized": False, "sources_verified": False, "disclaimer": DISCLAIMER}


def render_text(result):
    lines = [f"Capability: {result['capability']}", f"Description: {result['description']}", ""]
    for fw, e in result["frameworks"].items():
        lines += [fw.upper(), f"  Classification: {e['classification']}", f"  Trigger: {e['trigger_status'].value if isinstance(e['trigger_status'], Enum) else e['trigger_status']}", ""]
    lines += [f"Threshold crossed: {result['threshold_crossed']}", f"Deployment authorized: {result['deployment_authorized']}"]
    return "\n".join(lines)


def build_parser():
    p = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog="framework_compare")
    g = p.add_mutually_exclusive_group(required=True)
    g.add_argument("--list", action="store_true")
    g.add_argument("--all", action="store_true")
    g.add_argument("--capability")
    p.add_argument("--format", choices=("text", "json"), default="text")
    return p


def run(argv):
    err = io.StringIO()
    with contextlib.redirect_stderr(err):
        try:
            args = build_parser().parse_args(argv)
        except SystemExit as e:
            return e.code, err.getvalue().strip().splitlines()[-1]
    try:
        validate_table()
        if args.list:
            return 0, "\n".join(sorted(CAPABILITIES))
        results = [compare_capability(c) for c in sorted(CAPABILITIES)] if args.all else [compare_capability(args.capability)]
    except ValueError as e:
        return 1, f"error: {e}"
    if args.format == "json":
        return 0, json.dumps(results if args.all else results[0], indent=2, sort_keys=True, default=lambda o: o.value)
    return 0, "\n\n".join(render_text(r) for r in results)


class ComparisonTests(unittest.TestCase):
    def test_normalisation(self):
        self.assertEqual(normalize_capability(" Long Range-Autonomy "), "long_range_autonomy")

    def test_known_capability(self):
        self.assertEqual(compare_capability("sandbagging")["capability"], "sandbagging")

    def test_three_frameworks(self):
        self.assertEqual(set(compare_capability("cyber_uplift")["frameworks"]), FRAMEWORKS)

    def test_unknown_rejected(self):
        with self.assertRaises(ValueError):
            compare_capability("robotics")

    def test_no_threshold_claim(self):
        self.assertIsNone(compare_capability("ai_rd_automation")["threshold_crossed"])

    def test_no_authorisation(self):
        self.assertFalse(compare_capability("ai_rd_automation")["deployment_authorized"])

    def test_all_entries(self):
        self.assertEqual(sum(len(v) for v in POLICY_TABLE.values()), 21)

    def test_validate_ok(self):
        self.assertTrue(validate_table())

    def test_validate_fails_on_missing_framework(self):
        broken = {k: dict(v) for k, v in POLICY_TABLE.items()}
        del broken["sandbagging"]["anthropic"]
        with self.assertRaises(ValueError):
            validate_table(broken)

    def test_json_serialisable(self):
        self.assertIn("deployment_authorized", json.loads(run(["--capability", "sandbagging", "--format", "json"])[1]))

    def test_text_has_boundary_lines(self):
        self.assertIn("Deployment authorized: False", run(["--capability", "sandbagging"])[1])

    def test_self_improvement_is_separate(self):
        self.assertEqual(POLICY_TABLE["ai_self_improvement"]["openai"].classification, "Tracked Category")"}},{"type":"code","data":{"filename":"pf_1.py","headingEn":"main(): experiments","headingKn":"main(): ಪ್ರಯೋಗಗಳು","descEn":"main() runs the list and compare commands, JSON output, the error cases, validation, a count of cell types and twelve unit tests.","descKn":"main() list ಮತ್ತು compare ಆಜ್ಞೆಗಳು, JSON ಔಟ್‌ಪುಟ್, ದೋಷ ಪ್ರಕರಣಗಳು, ಮೌಲ್ಯೀಕರಣ, ಕೋಶ ಪ್ರಕಾರಗಳ ಎಣಿಕೆ ಮತ್ತು ಹನ್ನೆರಡು unit ಪರೀಕ್ಷೆ ಓಡಿಸುತ್ತದೆ.","code":"def main():
    section("1. Genuinely running: the command line")
    code, out = run(["--list"])
    print("--list exit", code)
    print(out)
    code, out = run(["--capability", "Long Range Autonomy"])
    print("\n--capability 'Long Range Autonomy' exit", code)
    print(out)
    print("the input was normalised to long_range_autonomy, each framework kept its own classification and trigger word, and the last two lines say that no threshold was assessed and nothing was authorised; the three classifications are the lesson's description and have not been checked against the source documents")

    section("2. Genuinely running: JSON output and the full set")
    code, out = run(["--capability", "sandbagging", "--format", "json"])
    data = json.loads(out)
    print("exit", code, "| keys:", sorted(data), "| threshold_crossed:", data["threshold_crossed"], "| sources_verified:", data["sources_verified"])
    code, out = run(["--all", "--format", "json"])
    data = json.loads(out)
    print("--all exit", code, "| capabilities:", len(data), "| entries:", sum(len(d["frameworks"]) for d in data))
    print("the JSON carries the same boundary fields and the full set holds 7 capabilities and 21 entries, and sources_verified is false in every report because no cell has been compared with the original text")

    section("3. Genuinely running: errors and argument conflicts")
    for argv in (["--capability", "robotics"], ["--capability", "AI research automation"], ["--all", "--capability", "sandbagging"], []):
        code, out = run(argv)
        print(f"{argv!s:42} exit {code}: {out}")
    print("an unknown capability exited 1 and listed the supported names, the phrase AI research automation was not guessed into ai_rd_automation because there is no alias table, and conflicting or missing arguments exited 2 with a usage error; an unknown input is never turned into a low-risk answer")

    section("4. Genuinely running: structural validation")
    broken = {k: dict(v) for k, v in POLICY_TABLE.items()}
    del broken["sandbagging"]["anthropic"]
    for label, table in (("complete table", None), ("one framework removed", broken)):
        try:
            print(f"{label}:", validate_table(table))
        except ValueError as e:
            print(f"{label}: ValueError: {e}")
    print("the complete table passed and the table with one framework removed failed by name; passing this check shows the table is well formed and says nothing about whether any entry is right")

    section("5. Genuinely counting: how many cells assert nothing")
    cells = [e for fws in POLICY_TABLE.values() for e in fws.values()]
    from collections import Counter
    print(dict(Counter(e.trigger_status.value for e in cells)))
    print("of the 21 cells, 7 say not_determined instead of asserting a classification, 5 are threshold dependent, 5 need a policy review and 4 say research category with no automatic trigger; leaving a cell undetermined is how the table avoids inventing an obligation it cannot source")

    section("6. Genuinely running: the twelve unit tests")
    stream = io.StringIO()
    res = unittest.TextTestRunner(stream=stream, verbosity=0).run(unittest.defaultTestLoader.loadTestsFromTestCase(ComparisonTests))
    print(f"ran {res.testsRun} tests | failures {len(res.failures)} | errors {len(res.errors)} | passed {res.wasSuccessful()}")
    print("the tests cover normalisation, the three-framework structure, the unknown-input error, the two boundary fields, the entry count, validation and its failure, JSON, text output and the separate self-improvement category on this lab's table, and they test the software and say nothing about the policies")"}},{"type":"output","data":{"output":"
